```

## Resource pattern (concrete)

A typical RadarLeb resource looks like this. Match this shape — don't reinvent.

```php
namespace App\Filament\Resources;

use App\Models\Game;
use Filament\Forms;
use Filament\Forms\Form;
use Filament\Resources\Resource;
use Filament\Tables;
use Filament\Tables\Table;

class GameResource extends Resource
{
    protected static ?string $model = Game::class;
    protected static ?string $navigationIcon = 'heroicon-o-trophy';
    protected static ?string $navigationGroup = 'Gameplay';

    public static function form(Form $form): Form
    {
        return $form->schema([
            Forms\Components\TextInput::make('name')->required(),
            Forms\Components\TextInput::make('price_to_play')
                ->numeric()
                ->required()
                ->helperText('Radar Cash units debited per scan (1, 4, 8, 24, 32)'),
            // price_to_play is Radar Cash units, not a dollar amount.
        ]);
    }

    public static function table(Table $table): Table
    {
        return $table
            ->columns([
                Tables\Columns\TextColumn::make('name')->searchable(),
                Tables\Columns\TextColumn::make('price_to_play')
                    ->label('Cost (Radar Cash)'),
                Tables\Columns\TextColumn::make('current_amount')
                    ->money('USD'),  // current_amount IS in USD-equivalent
            ])
            ->actions([Tables\Actions\EditAction::make()]);
    }

    public static function getPages(): array
    {
        return [
            'index'  => Pages\ListGames::route('/'),
            'create' => Pages\CreateGame::route('/create'),
            'edit'   => Pages\EditGame::route('/{record}/edit'),
        ];
    }
}
```

## Disabling actions intentionally

Many of our resources block create/delete because admins shouldn't add users
through the panel — that's seeders' job. Pattern:

```php
public static function canCreate(): bool { return false; }
public static function canEdit($record): bool { return true; }
public static function canDelete($record): bool { return false; }
```

If you see this on a resource, it's intentional. Don't "fix" it.

## Custom action — top-up wallet (concrete example)

`UserResource` has a `topoffRadarCash` action. Pattern for any custom admin
action that mutates state:

```php
Tables\Actions\Action::make('topoffRadarCash')
    ->label('Top up Radar Cash')
    ->icon('heroicon-o-banknotes')
    ->form([
        Forms\Components\TextInput::make('amount')
            ->numeric()->required()->minValue(1),
    ])
    ->action(function (User $record, array $data) {
        DB::transaction(function () use ($record, $data) {
            $record->wallet_balance += $data['amount'];
            $record->save();

            WalletTransaction::create([
                'user_id'  => $record->id,
                'amount'   => $data['amount'],
                'type'     => 'topup',
                'game_id'  => null,            // Top-ups have NO game
                'scan_id'  => null,
            ]);
        });

        Notification::make()
            ->title('Top-up complete')
            ->success()
            ->send();
    })
    ->requiresConfirmation();
```

Key rules in that action:
- `DB::transaction()` so the balance update + wallet row are atomic
- `game_id = null` for top-ups (see `docs/architecture.md` wallet rule #3)
- Use `Notification::make()` — never `dd()` or `flash()`
- `requiresConfirmation()` for any destructive or money-moving action

## Filtering by wallet history (the multi-game pattern)

The "Users by game" pages filter by `wallet_transactions.game_id`, NOT
`users.game_id`. This is because users can spend on multiple games. Pattern:

```php
// In e.g. app/Filament/Pages/MobileUsers.php
protected function getTableQuery(): Builder
{
    $gameId = Game::where('name', 'Mobile')->value('id');

    return User::query()
        ->whereHas('walletTransactions', function (Builder $q) use ($gameId) {
            $q->where('game_id', $gameId)
              ->whereIn('type', ['debit', 'play', 'spend']);
        });
}
```

Don't filter by `users.game_id` on these pages — that breaks multi-game
spending visibility. See `docs/history.md` for context.

## Widgets — keep queries bounded

Dashboard widgets (`StatsOverview`, `LatestWinners`, `ScansChart`) currently
have unbounded queries. When adding a new widget, always:

```php
// Bound the query
return Winner::query()
    ->latest('created_at')
    ->limit(10)
    ->with(['user:id,name', 'game:id,name'])  // Eager load + select only what you need
    ->get();
```

If a widget depends on `groupBy()`, add an explicit `limit()` after it. Don't
return unbounded data to the dashboard.

## After `composer update` or new Filament packages

```bash
php artisan filament:upgrade
```

This republishes `public/{js,css}/filament/`. Skip it and the admin panel
will render with broken styles after a dep bump.

## What NOT to do

- **Don't render Inertia/Vue inside Filament.** Different rendering pipelines.
- **Don't `dd()` or `var_dump()` inside an action handler.** It breaks the
  Livewire round-trip. Use `Notification::make()` for visible feedback or
  `Log::info()` for diagnostics.
- **Don't put `$` in front of `price_to_play`.** It's Radar Cash units.
- **Don't bypass `WalletTransaction::boot()` validation** by inserting via
  `DB::insert`. Always go through the Eloquent model.
- **Don't re-enable `canCreate()` on `UserResource` without thinking.** Users
  belong to seeders; admins don't create real customers via the panel.

